Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Solids and Others Industry, BREF LVIC-S (@ic-inorganic-solids: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_1M61GTSHDW8CPV4PNH48PTB4Y4
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Solids and Others Industry, BREF LVIC-S. adopted August 2007. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/large-volume-inorganic-chemicals-solids-and-others-industry).

The main detailed families include sodium carbonate/bicarbonate, titanium dioxide, carbon black, synthetic amorphous silica and inorganic phosphates. Other inorganic salts and mineral products receive different levels of detail.

Read the full general treatment and complete product chapters assigned in each case, retaining reaction routes, physical product state, feed quality, utilities, recovery, residues and differences in evidence depth. The whole-book route supports comparison across inorganic production systems.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled.

